  message: "Shipped in commit b2048af7d (in [Unreleased] of CHANGELOG, will land in v4.1.0). Producer migration for the four shape-3 edge-absent producers complete: r_lang.py:215 emits an imports Edge for library()/require() with src=make_file_id; astro.py:209 emits an imports Edge for frontmatter import statements (distinct from the existing component_ref imports Edge); make.py:282 emits an includes Edge for makefile include directives; blade.py emits an extends_template Edge for Blade @extends directives. All four producers' per-import / per-include / per-extends Symbols dropped. Audit-findings 0010 import / include / extends rows advance UNRESOLVED → PRELIM_RESOLVED. Tagging awaits_bakeoff_validation + for_deep_bakeoff per BVT discipline — the shape-3 redesign carries the same kind of structural-fold producer-migration claim as WI-zarov's Wave 4 PRs (the parent WI). Validation cohort design overlaps WI-zarov's: r_lang/astro/make/blade repos in DEEP Bundle 1 cover both items at once. Tracker hygiene correction: this item should have been advanced to done with these tags at PR-merge time per BVT discipline; the tags-and-status update was missed and is being applied retroactively as part of the 2026-05-07 sequence-planning audit."  # 0666
